# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# HR WORKSHOP  —  Wednesday 12 August 2026, 3:00–6:00 PM IST
# Prepared 2026-08-01. NOT YET APPLIED. Requires the Phase 0 / Phase 1 work.
#
# DESIGN (agreed 2026-08-01): the sheet IS the campaign.
#   env          → secrets + ONE pointer per campaign (SHEET_ID). Nothing else.
#   control tab  → the campaign itself: flow, event details, templates, switches.
#   code         → flow BEHAVIOUR (self_serve | sdr_assisted) + the frozen page.
#
# Adding next week's workshop = a new sheet + one env var. Ops set the date in
# the sheet, with no deploy. This is deliberate: EVENT_* was never set in
# .env.production, so the live campaign has been running on constants baked into
# config.ts — exactly the drift this removes.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# PART 1 — .env.production
# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# ⚠️ TODO — Tanu is creating a NEW sheet for this workshop. Do NOT reuse the
# Founder Workshop sheet (1qt-4O2Z0XiUetYitGd4aAVr60FPnH5XKgG1nhMT5IZ8).
#
# ⚠️ SHEET_ID=                      # new HR workshop spreadsheet ID
SHEET_CONTROL_TAB=control           # how the campaign config is FOUND — must stay
                                    # in env, since it cannot live inside the tab
                                    # it locates.
#
# Everything else formerly flipped per-campaign (EVENT_*, WATI_TPL_*, tab names)
# moves to the control tab in PART 2. Secrets stay here and never go in a sheet:
# WATI_ACCESS_TOKEN, GOOGLE_PRIVATE_KEY, AZURE_*, CRON_SECRET, SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL.
#
# Unchanged. LANDING_BASE_URL still serves the Event Pass (/api/pass?rid=) and the
# one-click unsubscribe (/api/unsubscribe?rid=), both linked from the messages, so
# this host must stay live even though the Meta form's CTA points at diacto.com.
LANDING_BASE_URL=https://workshop.diacto.com
#
# The landing page is FROZEN on the founder-workshop content by client request.
# It reads LANDING_EVENT_* (lib/event.ts), which default to literals — so set
# NOTHING here and the page holds exactly as it is today.


# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# PART 2 — `control` tab in the new sheet   (key | value, header row 1)
# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ── Campaign ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# key                  | value
# ---------------------|------------------------------------------------------
# flow                 | sdr_assisted
# campaign_label       | HR Workshop — 12 Aug 2026
# reg_id_prefix        | HRW                       → HRW-0812-####
#
# `flow: sdr_assisted` is what makes this campaign different, not a pile of
# switches. It means: form submission IS the registration (Confirmation Step 1),
# so the confirmation + PDF pass go out at INGEST; there is no booking link, no
# chasing ladder, and the landing page is out of the funnel. SDRs confirm by
# phone, and their dispositions return via the form tab's Remark column.

# ── Event  (CONFIRMED 2026-08-01, except venue) ──────────────────────────────
# event_date_label     | Wednesday, 12 August 2026
# event_date_short     | Wed, 12 August
# event_time_label     | 3:00 PM – 6:00 PM  (Check-in from 2:30 PM)   ⚠️ confirm check-in
# event_start_utc      | 2026-08-12T09:30:00Z
# ⚠️ event_venue       |                           ← NOT YET SUPPLIED
# ⚠️ event_map_url     |                           ← NOT YET SUPPLIED
#
# 12 Aug 2026 is a Wednesday; 15:00 IST = 09:30 UTC (verified).
# The day-before reminder is derived as event_start_utc − 29h → Tue 11 Aug,
# 10:00 IST (verified). That offset only lands at 10:00 because the event starts
# at 15:00 IST — if the time ever moves, the offset must become explicit.
#
# ⚠️ VENUE IS BLOCKING. Both templates print it in the body and Meta does not
# allow editing an approved template. BTB used "901, B Wing, Prabhavee Tech Park,
# Baner, Pune" — do NOT assume HR is the same.

# ── Auto-stop ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The campaign stops on its own once event_start_utc is reached — no manual flag
# to forget. After that: no ingest, no sends. Last week's sheet cannot quietly
# keep messaging people.

# ── Templates ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ⚠️ TODO — awaiting Anveshika's copy, then Meta approval. Approval took several
# days for BTB (wa_8_btb_two_hour_v3 was still PENDING days after submission),
# and the event is 11 days out. This is the critical path.
#
# THIS CAMPAIGN NEEDS ONLY TWO. No booking link, no ladder, no morning-of or
# 2-hour reminder.
#
# ⚠️ tpl_wa_confirmation |            ← sent at ingest, carries the Event Pass
# ⚠️ tpl_wa_reminder     |            ← one day before
# tpl_wa_lead_alert      | wa_lead_alert_full
#
# ⚠️⚠️ BOTH MUST BE SUBMITTED AS **UTILITY**, NOT MARKETING. ⚠️⚠️
# Measured on this number on 1 Aug 2026, the day Meta quality-restricted it:
#     UTILITY   — 30 sent,  0 failed
#     MARKETING — 36 sent, 25 failed  (41%)
# Nine registered attendees silently missed their 2-hour reminder purely because
# wa_two_hour was categorised MARKETING. A confirmation and an event reminder to
# someone who has already signed up are transactional. Category CANNOT be changed
# after approval — a mistake here means rebuilding and re-approving from scratch.
#
# wa_lead_alert_full stays: designation, company, employee count and location all
# arrive from the HR Instant Form. Only years_in_business is absent (the HR form
# does not ask it) and renders as "—".

# ── Switches  (existing behaviour, unchanged) ────────────────────────────────
# ingest_enabled       | TRUE
# nurture_enabled      | FALSE     ← no chasing ladder in this flow
# reminders_enabled    | TRUE
# email_enabled        | TRUE
# whatsapp_enabled     | TRUE
#
# FAIL DIRECTION differs by purpose, and the split is deliberate:
#   switches      → fail OPEN. Unreadable tab means "no opinion, carry on"; one
#                   transient Sheets blip must not silently kill a live campaign.
#   campaign cfg  → fail CLOSED. Unreadable or invalid event config means REFUSE
#                   TO SEND, and say so in Slack and /api/health. Falling back to
#                   a stale date would confidently message people about the wrong
#                   workshop, which is worse than sending nothing.


# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# PART 3 — sheet setup, before the first tick
# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
#   1. Share the sheet with the service account as EDITOR, or every write fails.
#   2. Create the `automation` tab with the exact header row. checkAutomationTable()
#      FAILS CLOSED — a missing column means the tick sends NOTHING rather than
#      risk double-messaging. Required:
#        lead_id · phone_key · email · confirm_token · registration_complete ·
#        nurture_stage · status · status_at
#      Plus the rest of the A map in lib/booking/service.ts: source, created_at,
#      name, designation, company, location, employee_count, years_in_business,
#      phone, reg_id, registered_at, last_nudge_at, pass_sent_at, reminders_sent,
#      expectations, status_source, last_reply, last_reply_at, promo_today, promo_day.
#   3. Create the `control` tab with `key` / `value` headers and the rows above.
#   4. Point `form_tab` at the tab Meta's connector writes into (control-tab
#      override, so it needs no deploy when the connector makes a new tab).
